{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftOneDimChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftOneDimChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_ne_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_ne_length","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L154-L158","doc":"**Non-vacuity II.**  The character is not `s ^ length` in general: the word\n`σ σ⁻¹` has writhe `0` and length `2`, so \"α_shift = letter count\" is a fact\nabout POSITIVE words and does not generalise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.abs_val_lt_length_of_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.abs_val_lt_length_of_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L140-L152","doc":"**Non-vacuity I.**  The bound is STRICT for a word containing a cancelling\npair — a genuine inequality, not an equality in disguise.\n\nNote the `(val s).natAbs = 1` hypothesis of `abs_val_le_length` is NOT needed\nhere: the writhe of `σ σ⁻¹` is zero, so the strictness holds for ANY generator\nvaluation.  Stated without it rather than carrying a decorative hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_conj","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L128-L138","doc":"The writhe is invariant under conjugating the word.  Together with the\nMarkov trace's own conjugation invariance, this is why the bound above is on\nthe REDUCED length rather than the written one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.abs_val_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.abs_val_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L118-L126","doc":"**The derived bound.**  When the generator has valuation `±1` — which is\nwhat the seminormal entries give at `ρ = ∓1` — the character's valuation is\nbounded by the word length.  This is `α_shift ≤ L`, obtained from the algebra\nrather than fitted to measurements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.abs_writhe_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.abs_writhe_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L110-L116","doc":"`|writhe| ≤ length`: each letter moves the writhe by exactly one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.val_charOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.val_charOf","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L91-L108","doc":"Under any additive valuation, the character's valuation is the writhe times\nthe generator's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_eq_zpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_eq_zpow","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L76-L89","doc":"**The closed form.**  On a one-dimensional channel the character of a word\nis `s` raised to its writhe — so such a channel sees the writhe and nothing\nelse about the word.  The all-row channel (`s = q`) and the all-column channel\n(`s = −q⁻¹`) are the two instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.charOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.charOf","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L70-L74","doc":"The character of a word on a one-dimensional channel whose generator acts\nby the scalar `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L65-L68","doc":"The writhe: `+1` per positive letter, `−1` per inverse letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Word","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/AlphaShiftOneDimChannel.lean#L61-L63","doc":"A braid word as a list of signed letters.  A one-dimensional channel sees\nonly each letter's sign, so that is all this carries. ","signatureChunk":0}]}